time=2026-10-19T20:25:46.499Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-d1d789de attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nThe provenance hooks command group and its install subcommand. Three\nfiles.\n\nWiring (cobra package):\n- cmd/provenance/hooks_cmd.go: a top-level group (createGroup), command\n  hooks, use \"hooks\", short \"Manage the provenance git hooks\", arity none.\n- cmd/provenance/hooks_install_cmd.go: a subcommand of hooks\n  (createSubcommand, parent hooks, command hooks-install), use \"install\",\n  short \"Install the pre-commit and commit-msg hooks (existing hooks are kept\n  as .bak)\", arity none, no flags.\n\nLogic, cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go (go package, package main).\nImports, each its own addImport, exactly these: fmt, io, os, path/filepath,\ngithub.com/spf13/cobra. Declarations:\n- const preCommitHook: a Go raw string literal (backquotes) whose content is\n  exactly the PRE-COMMIT text below, byte for byte, starting with\n  \"#!/bin/sh\" and ending with \"exit $exit_code\" and a final newline.\n- const commitMsgHook: likewise, exactly the COMMIT-MSG text below.\n- func installHook(dir, name, body string) (string, error): path :=\n  filepath.Join(dir, name). When the file exists with exactly body, return\n  \"unchanged\". When it exists with other content: if path+\".bak\" does not\n  exist, rename the file to path+\".bak\" (the first backup is kept: a\n  reinstall never replaces it); the result is \"replaced (previous hook kept\n  as <name>.bak)\", or \"replaced\" when a .bak already existed. When it does\n  not exist the result is \"installed\". Then os.MkdirAll(dir, 0o755) and\n  os.WriteFile(path, []byte(body), 0o755), and os.Chmod(path, 0o755).\n- func runHooksInstall(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string)\n  error: r, err := openRepo(cmd). dir, err := r.git(\"rev-parse\",\n  \"--git-path\", \"hooks\") (this honours core.hooksPath and worktrees); when\n  dir is relative, join it to r.Root. For pre-commit, commit-msg, then pre-push (prePushHook, a constant defined in hooks_pre_push_run.go) call installHook and return any error; the pre-push result is bound as `pushResult, err := installHook(dir, \"pre-push\", prePushHook)`. Then bind `mergeResult, err := ensureMergeDriver(r.Root)` (a helper that already exists in package main, in gitattributes_run.go: it makes git merge .provenance/versions.jsonl with provenance merge-manifest and returns \"created\", \"updated\" or \"unchanged\" plus an error) and return any error. Print \"\\n✓ Installed git hooks to\n  %s\\n\\n\" (dir), then \"  pre-commit (<result>):\\n    · Lints staged\n  provenance records (nearest .provenance.yml, else .linespec.yml)\\n    ·\n  Runs a record's associated specs when it moves open -> implemented\\n\\n\",\n  then \"  commit-msg (<result>):\\n    · Checks staged files against\n  provenance scope (provenance check --staged)\\n    · Validates provenance\n  tags, including [id@version]\\n\\n\", then \"  pre-push (<pushResult>):\n    · Runs pre_push_command (when the repository sets one) in a clean checkout of every pushed commit\n\n\", then \"  merge driver (<mergeResult>):\\n    · Merges .provenance/versions.jsonl with provenance merge-manifest (.gitattributes and git config)\\n\\n\", then \"  The hooks run $PROVENANCE,\n  else provenance on PATH.\\n\\n\". Return nil.\n\nHelpers that already exist in package main (call them; do not redefine\nthem): func ensureMergeDriver(root string) (string, error); func openRepo(cmd *cobra.Command) (*repo, error); type repo struct {\nRoot string; ... }; func (r *repo) git(args ...string) (string, error)\n(runs in r.Root and trims the output).\n\nPRE-COMMIT text (indented four spaces here; the constant has no indent):\n    #!/bin/sh\n    # provenance pre-commit hook, installed by `provenance hooks install`.\n    # Lints each staged provenance record with the config nearest to it, and runs\n    # a record's associated specs when it moves from open to implemented.\n\n    # $PROVENANCE, else provenance on PATH. Never a file in the repo: a\n    # hook must not run whatever is checked in under that name.\n    if [ -n \"$PROVENANCE\" ]; then\n        PROV=\"$PROVENANCE\"\n    elif command -v provenance >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n        PROV=\"provenance\"\n    else\n        echo \"provenance hook: no provenance binary. Set PROVENANCE or put provenance on PATH.\" >&2\n        exit 1\n    fi\n\n    staged=$(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACM | grep -E \"prov-[0-9]{4}-[^/]*\\.ya?ml$\" | grep -v \"/\\.versions/\")\n    if [ -z \"$staged\" ]; then\n        exit 0\n    fi\n\n    # Walk up from a file to the nearest .provenance.yml, else a .linespec.yml that\n    # has a provenance block (a LineSpec runner config is not a provenance root).\n    find_config() {\n        dir=$(dirname \"$1\")\n        while true; do\n            for name in .provenance.yml .linespec.yml; do\n                if [ -f \"$dir/$name\" ] && { [ \"$name\" = \".provenance.yml\" ] || grep -q '^provenance:' \"$dir/$name\"; }; then\n                    echo \"$dir/$name\"\n                    return 0\n                fi\n            done\n            if [ \"$dir\" = \".\" ] || [ \"$dir\" = \"/\" ]; then\n                return 1\n            fi\n            dir=$(dirname \"$dir\")\n        done\n    }\n\n    status_of() {\n        git show \"$1\" 2>/dev/null | grep \"^status:\" | head -1 | awk '{print $2}'\n    }\n\n    exit_code=0\n    for file in $staged; do\n        record=$(basename \"$file\" | sed -E 's/\\.ya?ml$//')\n        config=$(find_config \"$file\")\n        if [ -n \"$config\" ]; then\n            set -- -c \"$config\"\n        else\n            set --\n        fi\n        if ! \"$PROV\" \"$@\" lint --record \"$record\"; then\n            echo \"Commit blocked due to lint errors in $record\"\n            exit_code=1\n        fi\n        if [ \"$(status_of \"HEAD:$file\")\" = \"open\" ] && [ \"$(status_of \":$file\")\" = \"implemented\" ]; then\n            if ! \"$PROV\" \"$@\" run-specs --record \"$record\"; then\n                exit_code=1\n            fi\n        fi\n    done\n\n    exit $exit_code\n\nCOMMIT-MSG text (indented four spaces here; the constant has no indent):\n    #!/bin/sh\n    # provenance commit-msg hook, installed by `provenance hooks install`.\n    # Checks the staged files against provenance scope for every config they fall\n    # under. A config outside the root applies only when files under its\n    # directory are staged.\n\n    # $PROVENANCE, else provenance on PATH. Never a file in the repo: a\n    # hook must not run whatever is checked in under that name.\n    if [ -n \"$PROVENANCE\" ]; then\n        PROV=\"$PROVENANCE\"\n    elif command -v provenance >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n        PROV=\"provenance\"\n    else\n        echo \"provenance hook: no provenance binary. Set PROVENANCE or put provenance on PATH.\" >&2\n        exit 1\n    fi\n\n    COMMIT_MSG_FILE=\"$1\"\n\n    # A .linespec.yml is a root only when it has a provenance block.\n    dirs=$(find . \\( -name .provenance.yml -o -name .linespec.yml \\) -not -path \"./.git/*\" 2>/dev/null | while read -r f; do\n        case \"$f\" in\n            */.provenance.yml) echo \"$f\" ;;\n            *) grep -q '^provenance:' \"$f\" && echo \"$f\" ;;\n        esac\n    done | xargs -n1 dirname 2>/dev/null | sort -u)\n\n    if [ -z \"$dirs\" ]; then\n        if ! \"$PROV\" check --staged --message-file \"$COMMIT_MSG_FILE\"; then\n            echo \"\"\n            echo \"Commit blocked due to provenance scope violations\"\n            exit 1\n        fi\n        exit 0\n    fi\n\n    exit_code=0\n    for dir in $dirs; do\n        if [ -f \"$dir/.provenance.yml\" ]; then\n            config=\"$dir/.provenance.yml\"\n        else\n            config=\"$dir/.linespec.yml\"\n        fi\n        rel=$(echo \"$dir\" | sed 's|^\\./||')\n        if [ \"$rel\" != \".\" ]; then\n            if [ -z \"$(git diff --cached --name-only | grep \"^$rel/\" | head -1)\" ]; then\n                continue\n            fi\n        fi\n        if ! \"$PROV\" -c \"$config\" check --staged --message-file \"$COMMIT_MSG_FILE\"; then\n            exit_code=1\n        fi\n    done\n\n    if [ $exit_code -ne 0 ]; then\n        echo \"\"\n        echo \"Commit blocked due to provenance scope violations\"\n    fi\n\n    exit $exit_code\n\n## Constraints on it\n\n- All three files are grown by sedum-haiku (--only prov-2026-d1d789de): wiring with cobra, logic and the hook texts with go. Nothing in them is hand-written; a wrong result is fixed by revising this record and regrowing.\n- cmd/provenance/hooks_test.go is the hand-written gate: backups kept, reinstall keeps the first backup, and real commits through the installed hooks (built CLI) pass when tagged and in scope and are refused when untagged, out of scope, or when a record fails lint.\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nSelections made for this change on an earlier run (context only; they are not applied):\n\n- {\"action\":\"setArgs\",\"kwargs\":{\"arity\":\"none\",\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"hooks\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setArgs\",\"kwargs\":{\"arity\":\"none\",\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"hooks-install\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\",\"path\":\"fmt\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\",\"path\":\"io\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\",\"path\":\"os\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\",\"path\":\"path/filepath\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/spf13/cobra\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setConst\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"const preCommitHook = `#!/bin/sh\\n# provenance pre-commit hook, installed by ` + \\\"`\\\" + `provenance hooks install` + \\\"`\\\" + `.\\n# Lints each staged provenance record with the config nearest to it, and runs\\n# a record's associated specs when it moves from open to implemented.\\n\\n# $PROVENANCE, else provenance on PATH. Never a file in the repo: a\\n# hook must not run whatever is checked in under that name.\\nif [ -n \\\"$PROVENANCE\\\" ]; then\\n    PROV=\\\"$PROVENANCE\\\"\\nelif command -v provenance \\u003e/dev/null 2\\u003e\\u00261; then\\n    PROV=\\\"provenance\\\"\\nelse\\n    echo \\\"provenance hook: no provenance binary. Set PROVENANCE or put provenance on PATH.\\\" \\u003e\\u00262\\n    exit 1\\nfi\\n\\nstaged=$(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACM | grep -E \\\"prov-[0-9]{4}-[^/]*\\\\.ya?ml$\\\" | grep -v \\\"/\\\\.versions/\\\")\\nif [ -z \\\"$staged\\\" ]; then\\n    exit 0\\nfi\\n\\n# Walk up from a file to the nearest .provenance.yml, else a .linespec.yml that\\n# has a provenance block (a LineSpec runner config is not a provenance root).\\nfind_config() {\\n    dir=$(dirname \\\"$1\\\")\\n    while true; do\\n        for name in .provenance.yml .linespec.yml; do\\n            if [ -f \\\"$dir/$name\\\" ] \\u0026\\u0026 { [ \\\"$name\\\" = \\\".provenance.yml\\\" ] || grep -q '^provenance:' \\\"$dir/$name\\\"; }; then\\n                echo \\\"$dir/$name\\\"\\n                return 0\\n            fi\\n        done\\n        if [ \\\"$dir\\\" = \\\".\\\" ] || [ \\\"$dir\\\" = \\\"/\\\" ]; then\\n            return 1\\n        fi\\n        dir=$(dirname \\\"$dir\\\")\\n    done\\n}\\n\\nstatus_of() {\\n    git show \\\"$1\\\" 2\\u003e/dev/null | grep \\\"^status:\\\" | head -1 | awk '{print $2}'\\n}\\n\\nexit_code=0\\nfor file in $staged; do\\n    record=$(basename \\\"$file\\\" | sed -E 's/\\\\.ya?ml$//')\\n    config=$(find_config \\\"$file\\\")\\n    if [ -n \\\"$config\\\" ]; then\\n        set -- -c \\\"$config\\\"\\n    else\\n        set --\\n    fi\\n    if ! \\\"$PROV\\\" \\\"$@\\\" lint --record \\\"$record\\\"; then\\n        echo \\\"Commit blocked due to lint errors in $record\\\"\\n        exit_code=1\\n    fi\\n    if [ \\\"$(status_of \\\"HEAD:$file\\\")\\\" = \\\"open\\\" ] \\u0026\\u0026 [ \\\"$(status_of \\\":$file\\\")\\\" = \\\"implemented\\\" ]; then\\n        if ! \\\"$PROV\\\" \\\"$@\\\" run-specs --record \\\"$record\\\"; then\\n            exit_code=1\\n        fi\\n    fi\\ndone\\n\\nexit $exit_code\\n`\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\",\"name\":\"preCommitHook\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setConst\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"const commitMsgHook = `#!/bin/sh\\n# provenance commit-msg hook, installed by ` + \\\"`\\\" + `provenance hooks install` + \\\"`\\\" + `.\\n# Checks the staged files against provenance scope for every config they fall\\n# under. A config outside the root applies only when files under its\\n# directory are staged.\\n\\n# $PROVENANCE, else provenance on PATH. Never a file in the repo: a\\n# hook must not run whatever is checked in under that name.\\nif [ -n \\\"$PROVENANCE\\\" ]; then\\n    PROV=\\\"$PROVENANCE\\\"\\nelif command -v provenance \\u003e/dev/null 2\\u003e\\u00261; then\\n    PROV=\\\"provenance\\\"\\nelse\\n    echo \\\"provenance hook: no provenance binary. Set PROVENANCE or put provenance on PATH.\\\" \\u003e\\u00262\\n    exit 1\\nfi\\n\\nCOMMIT_MSG_FILE=\\\"$1\\\"\\n\\n# A .linespec.yml is a root only when it has a provenance block.\\ndirs=$(find . \\\\( -name .provenance.yml -o -name .linespec.yml \\\\) -not -path \\\"./.git/*\\\" 2\\u003e/dev/null | while read -r f; do\\n    case \\\"$f\\\" in\\n        */.provenance.yml) echo \\\"$f\\\" ;;\\n        *) grep -q '^provenance:' \\\"$f\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 echo \\\"$f\\\" ;;\\n    esac\\ndone | xargs -n1 dirname 2\\u003e/dev/null | sort -u)\\n\\nif [ -z \\\"$dirs\\\" ]; then\\n    if ! \\\"$PROV\\\" check --staged --message-file \\\"$COMMIT_MSG_FILE\\\"; then\\n        echo \\\"\\\"\\n        echo \\\"Commit blocked due to provenance scope violations\\\"\\n        exit 1\\n    fi\\n    exit 0\\nfi\\n\\nexit_code=0\\nfor dir in $dirs; do\\n    if [ -f \\\"$dir/.provenance.yml\\\" ]; then\\n        config=\\\"$dir/.provenance.yml\\\"\\n    else\\n        config=\\\"$dir/.linespec.yml\\\"\\n    fi\\n    rel=$(echo \\\"$dir\\\" | sed 's|^\\\\./||')\\n    if [ \\\"$rel\\\" != \\\".\\\" ]; then\\n        if [ -z \\\"$(git diff --cached --name-only | grep \\\"^$rel/\\\" | head -1)\\\" ]; then\\n            continue\\n        fi\\n    fi\\n    if ! \\\"$PROV\\\" -c \\\"$config\\\" check --staged --message-file \\\"$COMMIT_MSG_FILE\\\"; then\\n        exit_code=1\\n    fi\\ndone\\n\\nif [ $exit_code -ne 0 ]; then\\n    echo \\\"\\\"\\n    echo \\\"Commit blocked due to provenance scope violations\\\"\\nfi\\n\\nexit $exit_code\\n`\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\",\"name\":\"commitMsgHook\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func installHook(dir, name, body string) (string, error) {\\n\\tpath := filepath.Join(dir, name)\\n\\tresult := \\\"installed\\\"\\n\\tif existing, err := os.ReadFile(path); err == nil {\\n\\t\\tif string(existing) == body {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"unchanged\\\", nil\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif _, err := os.Stat(path + \\\".bak\\\"); os.IsNotExist(err) {\\n\\t\\t\\tif err := os.Rename(path, path+\\\".bak\\\"); err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tresult = \\\"replaced (previous hook kept as \\\" + name + \\\".bak)\\\"\\n\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\tresult = \\\"replaced\\\"\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err := os.MkdirAll(dir, 0o755); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err := os.WriteFile(path, []byte(body), 0o755); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err := os.Chmod(path, 0o755); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn result, nil\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\",\"name\":\"installHook\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func runHooksInstall(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\\n\\tr, err := openRepo(cmd)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tdir, err := r.git(\\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"--git-path\\\", \\\"hooks\\\")\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif !filepath.IsAbs(dir) {\\n\\t\\tdir = filepath.Join(r.Root, dir)\\n\\t}\\n\\tpreResult, err := installHook(dir, \\\"pre-commit\\\", preCommitHook)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tmsgResult, err := installHook(dir, \\\"commit-msg\\\", commitMsgHook)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tpushResult, err := installHook(dir, \\\"pre-push\\\", prePushHook)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \\\"\\\\n✓ Installed git hooks to %s\\\\n\\\\n\\\", dir)\\n\\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \\\"  pre-commit (%s):\\\\n    · Lints staged provenance records (nearest .provenance.yml, else .linespec.yml)\\\\n    · Runs a record's associated specs when it moves open -\\u003e implemented\\\\n\\\\n\\\", preResult)\\n\\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \\\"  commit-msg (%s):\\\\n    · Checks staged files against provenance scope (provenance check --staged)\\\\n    · Validates provenance tags, including [id@version]\\\\n\\\\n\\\", msgResult)\\n\\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \\\"  pre-push (%s):\\\\n    · Runs pre_push_command (when the repository sets one) in a clean checkout of every pushed commit\\\\n\\\\n\\\", pushResult)\\n\\tfmt.Fprint(out, \\\"  The hooks run $PROVENANCE, else provenance on PATH.\\\\n\\\\n\\\")\\n\\treturn nil\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\",\"name\":\"runHooksInstall\"}}\n\n## Already present\n\nThese regions already exist in the files below and belong to other changes. Do not select them: an action that resolves to one of them would conflict with the change that owns it.\n\n- cmd/provenance/hooks_cmd.go: registerSubcommand