on, signature and body, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The function's name.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"decls\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"code\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setMethod\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one method, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole method declaration, receiver, signature and body, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The method's name.\"\n        },\n        \"receiver\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The receiver's type name, without a pointer star.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"decls\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"code\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setType\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one named type, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole type declaration, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The type's name.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"decls\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"code\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setVar\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one package-level variable, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole var declaration, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The variable's name.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"decls\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"code\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"
time=2026-10-19T20:26:05.974Z level=INFO msg="model responded" record=prov-2026-d1d789de attempt=1 response="{\"invocations\": [{\"action\": \"createGroup\", \"kwargs\": {\"bin\": \"provenance\", \"command\": \"hooks\", \"short\": \"Manage the provenance git hooks\", \"use\": \"hooks\"}}, {\"action\": \"createSubcommand\", \"kwargs\": {\"bin\": \"provenance\", \"command\": \"hooks-install\", \"parent\": \"hooks\", \"short\": \"Install the pre-commit and commit-msg hooks (existing hooks are kept as .bak)\", \"use\": \"install\"}}, {\"action\": \"setArgs\", \"kwargs\": {\"arity\": \"none\", \"bin\": \"provenance\", \"command\": \"hooks\"}}, {\"action\": \"setArgs\", \"kwargs\": {\"arity\": \"none\", \"bin\": \"provenance\", \"command\": \"hooks-install\"}}, {\"action\": \"addImport\", \"kwargs\": {\"file\": \"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\", \"path\": \"fmt\"}}, {\"action\": \"addImport\", \"kwargs\": {\"file\": \"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\", \"path\": \"io\"}}, {\"action\": \"addImport\", \"kwargs\": {\"file\": \"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\", \"path\": \"os\"}}, {\"action\": \"addImport\", \"kwargs\": {\"file\": \"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\", \"path\": \"path/filepath\"}}, {\"action\": \"addImport\", \"kwargs\": {\"file\": \"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\", \"path\": \"github.com/spf13/cobra\"}}, {\"action\": \"setConst\", \"kwargs\": {\"code\": \"const preCommitHook = `#!/bin/sh\\n# provenance pre-commit hook, installed by ` + \\\"`\\\" + `provenance hooks install` + \\\"`\\\" + `.\\n# Lints each staged provenance record with the config nearest to it, and runs\\n# a record's associated specs when it moves from open to implemented.\\n\\n# $PROVENANCE, else provenance on PATH. Never a file in the repo: a\\n# hook must not run whatever is checked in under that name.\\nif [ -n \\\"$PROVENANCE\\\" ]; then\\n    PROV=\\\"$PROVENANCE\\\"\\nelif command -v provenance \\u003e/dev/null 2\\u003e\\u00261; then\\n    PROV=\\\"provenance\\\"\\nelse\\n    echo \\\"provenance hook: no provenance binary. Set PROVENANCE or put provenance on PATH.\\\" \\u003e\\u00262\\n    exit 1\\nfi\\n\\nstaged=$(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACM | grep -E \\\"prov-[0-9]{4}-[^/]*\\\\.ya?ml$\\\" | grep -v \\\"/\\\\.versions/\\\")\\nif [ -z \\\"$staged\\\" ]; then\\n    exit 0\\nfi\\n\\n# Walk up from a file to the nearest .provenance.yml, else a .linespec.yml that\\n# has a provenance block (a LineSpec runner config is not a provenance root).\\nfind_config() {\\n    dir=$(dirname \\\"$1\\\")\\n    while true; do\\n        for name in .provenance.yml .linespec.yml; do\\n            if [ -f \\\"$dir/$name\\\" ] \\u0026\\u0026 { [ \\\"$name\\\" = \\\".provenance.yml\\\" ] || grep -q '^provenance:' \\\"$dir/$name\\\"; }; then\\n                echo \\\"$dir/$name\\\"\\n                return 0\\n            fi\\n        done\\n        if [ \\\"$dir\\\" = \\\".\\\" ] || [ \\\"$dir\\\" = \\\"/\\\" ]; then\\n            return 1\\n        fi\\n        dir=$(dirname \\\"$dir\\\")\\n    done\\n}\\n\\nstatus_of() {\\n    git show \\\"$1\\\" 2\\u003e/dev/null | grep \\\"^status:\\\" | head -1 | awk '{print $2}'\\n}\\n\\nexit_code=0\\nfor file in $staged; do\\n    record=$(basename \\\"$file\\\" | sed -E 's/\\\\.ya?ml$//')\\n    config=$(find_config \\\"$file\\\")\\n    if [ -n \\\"$config\\\" ]; then\\n        set -- -c \\\"$config\\\"\\n    else\\n        set --\\n    fi\\n    if ! \\\"$PROV\\\" \\\"$@\\\" lint --record \\\"$record\\\"; then\\n        echo \\\"Commit blocked due to lint errors in $record\\\"\\n        exit_code=1\\n    fi\\n    if [ \\\"$(status_of \\\"HEAD:$file\\\")\\\" = \\\"open\\\" ] \\u0026\\u0026 [ \\\"$(status_of \\\":$file\\\")\\\" = \\\"implemented\\\" ]; then\\n        if ! \\\"$PROV\\\" \\\"$@\\\" run-specs --record \\\"$record\\\"; then\\n            exit_code=1\\n        fi\\n    fi\\ndone\\n\\nexit $exit_code\\n`\", \"file\": \"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\", \"name\": \"preCommitHook\"}}, {\"action\": \"setConst\", \"kwargs\": {\"code\": \"const commitMsgHook = `#!/bin/sh\\n# provenance commit-msg hook, installed by ` + \\\"`\\\" + `provenance hooks install` + \\\"`\\\" + `.\\n# Checks the staged files against provenance scope for every config they fall\\n# under. A config outside the root applies only when files under its\\n# directory are staged.\\n\\n# $PROVENANCE, else provenance on PATH. Never a file in the repo: a\\n# hook must not run whatever is checked in under that name.\\nif [ -n \\\"$PROVENANCE\\\" ]; then\\n    PROV=\\\"$PROVENANCE\\\"\\nelif command -v provenance \\u003e/dev/null 2\\u003e\\u00261; then\\n    PROV=\\\"provenance\\\"\\nelse\\n    echo \\\"provenance hook: no provenance binary. Set PROVENANCE or put provenance on PATH.\\\" \\u003e\\u00262\\n    exit 1\\nfi\\n\\nCOMMIT_MSG_FILE=\\\"$1\\\"\\n\\n# A .linespec.yml is a root only when it has a provenance block.\\ndirs=$(find . \\\\( -name .provenance.yml -o -name .linespec.yml \\\\) -not -path \\\"./.git/*\\\" 2\\u003e/dev/null | while read -r f; do\\n    case \\\"$f\\\" in\\n        */.provenance.yml) echo \\\"$f\\\" ;;\\n        *) grep -q '^provenance:' \\\"$f\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 echo \\\"$f\\\" ;;\\n    esac\\ndone | xargs -n1 dirname 2\\u003e/dev/null | sort -u)\\n\\nif [ -z \\\"$dirs\\\" ]; then\\n    if ! \\\"$PROV\\\" check --staged --message-file \\\"$COMMIT_MSG_FILE\\\"; then\\n        echo \\\"\\\"\\n        echo \\\"Commit blocked due to provenance scope violations\\\"\\n        exit 1\\n    fi\\n    exit 0\\nfi\\n\\nexit_code=0\\nfor dir in $dirs; do\\n    if [ -f \\\"$dir/.provenance.yml\\\" ]; then\\n        config=\\\"$dir/.provenance.yml\\\"\\n    else\\n        config=\\\"$dir/.linespec.yml\\\"\\n    fi\\n    rel=$(echo \\\"$dir\\\" | sed 's|^\\\\./||')\\n    if [ \\\"$rel\\\" != \\\".\\\" ]; then\\n        if [ -z \\\"$(git diff --cached --name-only | grep \\\"^$rel/\\\" | head -1)\\\" ]; then\\n            continue\\n        fi\\n    fi\\n    if ! \\\"$PROV\\\" -c \\\"$config\\\" check --staged --message-file \\\"$COMMIT_MSG_FILE\\\"; then\\n        exit_code=1\\n    fi\\ndone\\n\\nif [ $exit_code -ne 0 ]; then\\n    echo \\\"\\\"\\n    echo \\\"Commit blocked due to provenance scope violations\\\"\\nfi\\n\\nexit $exit_code\\n`\", \"file\": \"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\", \"name\": \"commitMsgHook\"}}, {\"action\": \"setFunction\", \"kwargs\": {\"code\": \"func installHook(dir, name, body string) (string, error) {\\n\\tpath := filepath.Join(dir, name)\\n\\tresult := \\\"installed\\\"\\n\\tif existing, err := os.ReadFile(path); err == nil {\\n\\t\\tif string(existing) == body {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"unchanged\\\", nil\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif _, err := os.Stat(path + \\\".bak\\\"); os.IsNotExist(err) {\\n\\t\\t\\tif err := os.Rename(path, path+\\\".bak\\\"); err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tresult = \\\"replaced (previous hook kept as \\\" + name + \\\".bak)\\\"\\n\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\tresult = \\\"replaced\\\"\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err := os.MkdirAll(dir, 0o755); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err := os.WriteFile(path, []byte(body), 0o755); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err := os.Chmod(path, 0o755); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn result, nil\\n}\", \"file\": \"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\", \"name\": \"installHook\"}}, {\"action\": \"setFunction\", \"kwargs\": {\"code\": \"func runHooksInstall(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\\n\\tr, err := openRepo(cmd)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tdir, err := r.git(\\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"--git-path\\\", \\\"hooks\\\")\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif !filepath.IsAbs(dir) {\\n\\t\\tdir = filepath.Join(r.Root, dir)\\n\\t}\\n\\tpreResult, err := installHook(dir, \\\"pre-commit\\\", preCommitHook)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tmsgResult, err := installHook(dir, \\\"commit-msg\\\", commitMsgHook)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tpushResult, err := installHook(dir, \\\"pre-push\\\", prePushHook)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tmergeResult, err := ensureMergeDriver(r.Root)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \\\"\\\\n✓ Installed git hooks to %s\\\\n\\\\n\\\", dir)\\n\\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \\\"  pre-commit (%s):\\\\n    · Lints staged provenance records (nearest .provenance.yml, else .linespec.yml)\\\\n    · Runs a record's associated specs when it moves open -\\u003e implemented\\\\n\\\\n\\\", preResult)\\n\\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \\\"  commit-msg (%s):\\\\n    · Checks staged files against provenance scope (provenance check --staged)\\\\n    · Validates provenance tags, including [id@version]\\\\n\\\\n\\\", msgResult)\\n\\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \\\"  pre-push (%s):\\\\n    · Runs pre_push_command (when the repository sets one) in a clean checkout of every pushed commit\\\\n\\\\n\\\", pushResult)\\n\\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \\\"  merge driver (%s):\\\\n    · Merges .provenance/versions.jsonl with provenance merge-manifest (.gitattributes and git config)\\\\n\\\\n\\\", mergeResult)\\n\\tfmt.Fprint(out, \\\"  The hooks run $PROVENANCE, else provenance on PATH.\\\\n\\\\n\\\")\\n\\treturn nil\\n}\", \"file\": \"cmd/provenance/hooks_install_run.go\", \"name\": \"runHooksInstall\"}}]}" prompt_tokens=17232 completion_tokens=6114
